00:00:04.639 --> 00:00:05.617
- [Lina] She what?

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:06.450
- [Group] She punch.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.283
- She elbow.

00:00:07.283 --> 00:00:08.116
- [Group] She elbow.

00:00:08.116 --> 00:00:08.949
- She kick.

00:00:08.949 --> 00:00:09.910
- [Group] She kick.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:10.743
- SheFighter.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:11.704
- [Group] SheFighter.

00:00:11.704 --> 00:00:13.211
(clapping)

00:00:13.211 --> 00:00:16.047
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.047 --> 00:00:17.574
(huffing)

00:00:17.574 --> 00:00:19.707
- My name is Lina Khalifeh.

00:00:19.707 --> 00:00:22.797
I'm the owner and founder of SheFighter,

00:00:22.797 --> 00:00:26.885
the first self-defense studio
for women in the Middle East.

00:00:26.885 --> 00:00:30.536
I teach a mix between taekwondo, boxing

00:00:30.536 --> 00:00:33.475
and pure self-defense techniques.

00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:36.205
We also empower women through
seminars and workshops,

00:00:36.205 --> 00:00:39.035
like domestic violence, sexual harassment,

00:00:39.035 --> 00:00:41.435
assault and also women empowerment.

00:00:41.435 --> 00:00:44.018
(upbeat music)

00:00:46.187 --> 00:00:49.035
I started in 2004
because one of my friends

00:00:49.035 --> 00:00:52.265
got abused by her father and brothers.

00:00:52.265 --> 00:00:54.776
I was really upset about her situation.

00:00:54.776 --> 00:00:56.915
Because I have a
background in martial arts,

00:00:56.915 --> 00:01:01.747
I decided to start giving lessons
for women in self-defense.

00:01:01.747 --> 00:01:04.456
Domestic violence is a
high percent in Jordan,

00:01:04.456 --> 00:01:06.555
in violence for women.

00:01:06.555 --> 00:01:09.627
We have street harassment,
you don't see lots of girls

00:01:09.627 --> 00:01:13.139
walking the street because of that.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.889
(ethereal music)

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.365
SheFighter is safe
place for women to come

00:01:21.365 --> 00:01:23.374
and talk about their issues because

00:01:23.374 --> 00:01:27.455
all the other girls have been
mostly the same experience.

00:01:27.455 --> 00:01:29.965
The physical training and mental training

00:01:29.965 --> 00:01:31.656
both are really important.

00:01:31.656 --> 00:01:35.823
So we start with talking to
the girls about their stories,

00:01:37.085 --> 00:01:39.267
then we move to the training.

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:43.434
We have trained and empowered
more than 12,000 women.

00:01:44.295 --> 00:01:46.995
(heavy bass music)

00:01:46.995 --> 00:01:48.835
- Before I joined, I was facing

00:01:48.835 --> 00:01:50.825
like, a lot of verbal harassment.

00:01:50.825 --> 00:01:55.005
I felt so weak because I
couldn't do anything about it.

00:01:55.005 --> 00:01:58.201
Since I joined, verbal
harassment is less now,

00:01:58.201 --> 00:01:59.853
because I'm more confident now,

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.261
so when walking in street, that shows,

00:02:02.261 --> 00:02:04.761
that reflects to other people.

00:02:06.841 --> 00:02:09.282
- Most girls here, after the training,

00:02:09.282 --> 00:02:13.282
they feel that they can
stand up for themselves.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.493
It's about providing them
with the self-defense skills

00:02:17.493 --> 00:02:21.660
to defend their rights and
to have a voice in society.

